task: intent-span-runaway (a decoder-side guard on a Reading: grounded in the message, no two spans over one stretch)
agent: okay-42
started: 2026-09-07
branch: feature/intent-span-runaway

why: BACKLOG intent-span-runaway: one live run answered a nine-word
  message with twenty spans cycling four intents; nothing bounds the
  count. Grounding (every span's text is in the message) held 12/12 and
  would not have caught it -- the texts were real substrings -- so the
  guard is DISTINCTNESS: no two kept spans covering the same stretch of
  the message, grounding beside it as the cheap check. `Reading.grounded
  (message)` in Classify.scala, laws in TestClassify (the twenty-span
  cycle collapses, an ungrounded span drops, a clean reading is the
  identity), the live suite applies it before counting. `decide` does
  not change.
